.TH INTERFERE 1
.SH NAME
interfere \- find colliding parts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B interfere
.I assembly.fold
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Interfere
prints a line for each pair of colliding parts:
.PP
.RS
.I "name name"
.B points
.I n
.RE
.PP
The material of each part is sampled on a 1 mm grid of its flat faces,
at three depths.
A sample collides if it lies inside the other part, 1 um or more from
its faces; parts that only touch do not collide.
.I N
is the number of colliding samples, counted up to a limit.
.SH SEE ALSO
place(1)
.SH BUGS
An overlap thinner than the grid may be missed.
